remain stable and not to advance until the load reaches Gc, which is larger than the value, 2 , predicted by Griffith’s theory.12 For example, lattice trapping for 111 and 110 fracture in Si has been studied with electronic structure calculations based on the density functional theory DFT .12 In the 111 brittle fracture, cleavagelike crack propagation occurs in a small range of G above Gc. At larger values of G, crack propagation becomes unstable against surfacestep formation due to slip, as shown in Fig. 2 b . The slip
